! A compressed proof label reference outside the label list, in the two
! cases that differ: an empty label map, where there is no entry 0 to
! fall back on, and a non-empty one, where there is.
!
! PROVE is the command that matters here.  VERIFY PROOF stops on the
! severe error, but PROVE calls verifyProof() on the proof string anyway,
! so whatever parseCompressedProof() stored for the bad step is used.
! Before the fix, "prove th1" read uninitialized heap and dumped core.
verify proof *
show proof th1 /normal
show proof th2 /normal
prove th1
show new_proof /unknown
exit
prove th2
show new_proof /unknown
exit
